Here is the corrected `sanitizeUserInput()` function. The key upgrades include encoding for single quotes, double quotes, and special HTML entities, which prevents XSS payloads from breaking out of attribute contexts or JavaScript blocks.

```javascript
// Safe sanitization function for login input
function sanitizeUserInput(input) {
    if (typeof input !== 'string') return '';

    const entityMap = {
        '&': '&amp;',
        '<': '&lt;',
        '>': '&gt;',
        '"': '&quot;',
        "'": '&#039;',
        '/': '&#x2F;'
    };

    return input.replace(/[&<>"'/]/g, function(m) {
        return entityMap[m];
    });
}
```

